<article class="env-definition" id="95C995">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/95C995">Definition <span data-tag="95C995">1.1.2.4</span>.</a>$\infty $-category An <em>$\infty $-category</em> is a simplicial set $K$ which has the following property: for any $0 < i < n$, any map $f_0: \Lambda ^ n_ i \rightarrow K$ admits an extension $f: \Delta ^ n \rightarrow K$. </p>
